  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "After the most recent update, at so far relatively random the IK will offset slightly by rotation, this is temporarily fixed by locomoting using the left controller, it is not corrected by rotating.\n\nI have so far been able to reproduce it semi-regularly by moving my head around at random, the IK would shortly after do an offset at a range of anything between 10 to 30 degrees.\n\nI was able to also confirm that other users see the same offset on me.\n\nThe first attached image shows the offset without any indicators, the second image shows the offset by being near a trigger, which shows the controller's real positions, the highlighted controllers matches what SteamVR sees aswell, so it is not a SteamVR tracking issue.\n\nThe second image is also not the IK stretching too far. I have so far tested it on two very different rigs, with slightly different regularities.\n\nI am using Knuckles DV units incase that may have something to do with it.\n\nI have not tested if this occurs in Fullbody yet.",
